Z||000022||rogergarrison||05-19-2000||01:12 PM||||OK, (from a project engineer on Fiero) the prototype was a scratch built V8 power car, Pontiac wanted its own Marque 'Corvette'. Higher ups in GM stated NO-corvette would forever be its ONLY sports car! so in rethinking the engineers transformed it to a urban transportation cheap car and GM okd that if they scrapped all the hi-tech parts and made it mechanicaly from off the shelf parts (read as Citation drive train, Chevette Front assby). As the car buyers started buying, they made them sportier (v6,GT models) but the rep killed sales in 88. The great shame was the 89 would have had the 3.8 turbo as in Buick Grand National, as an option. Now that would have been fun, corvette killer.||||reg||1
