Z||000028||Fiero Jon||05-21-2000||07:49 PM||||Where to begin?  <P>First, every GM car out sells the Vette in every year.  If the Vette was a car they made 100,000 of every year, they wouldn't be worth anything.  The Vette is seen as the "pinnacle" of GM, and as such it isn't going away.  The C6 Vette (due out in approx. 2004-5) is rumored to either carry the new LS-4 engine, or less likely the Cadillac EVOQ 425 hp, supercharged Northstar.  <P>As far as the Fiero's demise.  No one, but the engineers know what was coming in 1989.  Most likely the outside would have been superficial changes.  Look at the Firebird, Pontiac likes to change outward appearance every year, with a facelift about every 5-6 years.  It keeps every year 'special' and distinctive.  The engine offerings would have most likely been the 3.1 or 3.4 DOHC in the SE, GT, or Formula, but probably would have remained the 2.8.  With a base engine remaining the 2.5.  How did I arrive at this?  Look at the other engines offered by Pontiac at the time.  <P>An article I read in 1990 about the Fiero and it's demise stated a few reasons that I can remember.  The VP that liked the Fiero left around the end of the 1987 model year, and with no support in management--gone.  The stigma of the "fire problem" was a sore spot.  The sales did not match projections, GM has a habit of killing cars that don't sell 300,000 units.  (Vette excluded, and look at the F-body crisis now).  And remeber the Fiero was market as a "commuter" car, not a sportscar.  <P>And lastly, from my own opinion, GM loves to kill off cars just as they're getting interesting--Pontiac Fiero, Cadillac Allante', Chevy Corvair--just to name a few.  Sorry to say the Fiero probably would have been around longer if Ford or Chrysler had built them.  But, I like the exclusivity of mine as they aren't seen every day--like all those "riceboy" cars.||||reg||5
Z||000029||ounmongk||05-21-2000||08:10 PM||||YEAH! death to all ricey cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (well, just the civics)<BR>On a sentimental note, everyone, shouldn't we talk about something other than how the fiero line became extinct? poor ole' red here is getting teary. on a FURTHER note, I hear Nissan is planning to bring the Z back into production? is this true? perhaps there's hope for us fieroites.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> there's plenty of old models that have been resurrected... charger, prowler, malibu, Cher  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (oops), hmm I'm sure there's more though...  perhaps the fiero will come back in a buff new body, eh? (never hurts to dream)   ||||reg||1
